AB  - AeroTitan Stone: Advanced Engineering Records Technical Disclosure & Priority Verification: This record serves as the formal evidence of priority for a breakthrough innovation in Advanced Composite Material Science. The technology introduces a next-generation High-Performance Engineered Stone (branded as AeroTitan) that redefines the standards of durability and weight in the construction industry. Performance Benchmarks (Verified Results): Ultra-High Strength: The material delivers a certified compressive strength of 55 MPa, ensuring structural integrity under extreme conditions and heavy-duty applications. Lightweight Engineering: Engineered with a specialized density of 1.74, this product is 30% lighter than conventional natural and synthetic stones, offering significant strategic advantages in logistics and reducing the dead load of architectural structures. Impact-Absorbing Matrix (Unbreakable): Unlike standard brittle materials, this technology features a Non-Fragile structural behavior. Its internal architecture is designed to resist high-impact forces without catastrophic fracturing—a unique property achieved through a proprietary reinforcement system. Legal Integrity & IP Protection: The documents provided (related to Application No. 139650140003003809) confirm that the innovation has cleared the Global Prior Art Examination, establishing its worldwide uniqueness. The registration process was intentionally maintained at the strategic priority stage to ensure the confidentiality of the proprietary formulation (Know-how) and to protect trade secrets from unauthorized public disclosure. Strategic Vision: This official disclosure is part of a global technology transfer initiative, specifically targeting the industrial hub of Pune, India, for mass manufacturing and international distribution to global infrastructure markets. Keywords (Tags): AeroTitan Stone, Advanced Composite Materials, Unbreakable Stone Technology, 55 MPa High-Strength Stone, Lightweight Construction Materials, Technology Transfer India, Impact Resistant Infrastructure, Proprietary Engineering
