AB  - Konya province is one important marble production centres of Türkiye and has marble quarries in various regions.Productivity in the marble quarries in the region has increased with investments made in recent years, while environmentally friendly mining practices are becoming increasingly widespread, and efforts are being made to minimize environmental impacts.Marble production in the region makes significant contributions to both the Konya economy and natural stone exports of Türkiye.Although marble quarries have an important place in natural stone production, they can lead to various negative environmental impacts.Extensive excavation and cutting operations are carried out during the opening of marble quarries, which disrupts the natural ecosystem.Quarries opened in forested areas can negatively affect natural life by leading to tree felling and the destruction of vegetation.The intense dust generated during cutting reduces air quality, affecting both the health of workers and the surrounding agricultural lands.These dust particles can spread into the environment through the wind, contaminating water sources and reducing soil fertility quality.Water usage is also a significant environmental problem in marble quarries.Large amounts of water are consumed during cutting and processing activity, leading to depletion of groundwater and surface water.Furthermore, contamination of water used during cutting with marble dust and chemicals can degrade the quality of water sources, harming the ecosystem in the region.Discharging untreated wastewater into the environment can cause surrounding water sources to become filled with mud and stone dust.Noise pollution is another major problem encountered in marble quarries.Cutting machines, blasting operations, and stone handling vehicles generate high levels of noise, negatively impacting the health of workers and reducing the quality of life for people living in the surrounding area.Large quantities of stone and soil waste generated during marble production, if not properly managed, can lead to the accumulation of large waste piles in the environment.The pollution caused during the storage and transportation of this waste makes land use difficult and causes visual pollution.In recent years, sustainable mining practices have become widespread in marble quarries to reduce environmental impacts.Environmental damage is minimized through measures such as water-saving closed-loop systems, irrigation methods for dust control, recycling processes, and rehabilitation projects.However, more widespread and effective implementation of these measures is crucial in reducing the negative environmental impacts of marble production.
