AB  - This research examines the potential use of Waste Marble Powder (WMP) as a green binder for stabilizing fine-grained soils, addressing two important problems simultaneously. The effect of varying the amount of WMP (0%, 5%, 10%, 15%, and 20%) on the Atterberg limits, compaction, UCS, CBR, and volume of soil was assessed through an extensive experimental program. The investigations showed that the geotechnical properties of the soil improved greatly when around 10–15% WMP was added. The plasticity index, swelling, shrinkage, and overall strength of the specimens drop noticeably and their load-bearing capacity increases. Using ANOVA and regression modeling showed that the main results were reliable and significant. Overall, the paper states that WMP is a sustainable replacement for regular soil stabilizers used in subgrade improvement in geotechnical projects.
