AB  - This paper discuss the main mineral resources of Cuba. In the metallic resources the iron-nickel-cobalt lateritic ore deposits are the most important and constitute the major reserves in the country. There are also other small deposits of chromite, copper, manganese, and magnetite iron. Important mineral deposits of lead and zinc of significative tonnage occur in the western part of the island. Small mineral deposits of refractory type represent the gold-silver mineralization. The main industrial minerals correspond to dimension stones, clay minerals deposits, phosphate bearing rocks, zeolites, feldspar, quartz, gypsum and salt rocks. With the exception of the iron-nickel-cobalt resources, the most ore deposits in Cuba can be considered as small mineral deposits developed by small-scale mining. In this sense it imply relative small capital investment, small output and low turn over as principal features. The present paper tend to explain the main metallic and non metallic resources in Cuba
