AB  - Summary Within Podillia (Ternopil, Khmelnytskyi, Vinnytsia regions), there are no mineral resources that have not been affected by mining. Some of them – phosphorites, flint, gypsum – are almost exhausted, peat reserves are depleted, and in some regions (Vinnytsia and Ternopil) – limestone, chalk and even sand. This has led to the gradual formation in Podillia of a unique, as yet little-studied geological and geomorphological group of anthropogenic protected sites, which includes: ancient and unique deposits of certain types of minerals in Podillia: sandstones near Terebovlia in the Ternopil region; limestone within the Podillia Tovtry; granite in the Middle Pobuzhzhia; waste rock dumps, mines (quarries), and quarries as original geological sections and landforms. Detailed knowledge of these objects and justification of their significance through the study of their formation history will make it possible to include anthropogenic geological objects in the general system of protected objects in Podillia.
