AB  - In this study, heavy metals originating from industrial wastes which contaminate groundwater have been investigated. The studied industrial wastes are fly ash, marble dust, boron waste, and silica fume and these wastes were mixed at different proportions with selected soil. These mixtures were compacted into permeameter cell and seepage test was performed. The leachates were analyzed to determine heavy metals. The measured heavy metal quantities were compared with the limit values in the relevant standards. The results revealed that quantitative values of the heavy metals from the leachates were determined to be within the allowable limits, except for arsenic and chromium. Furthermore, the results showed that As and Cr were detected at trace level for mixtures that contained FA and this confirmed FA fittingly for absorption of heavy metals with anti-pollution effects.
