AB  - Abstract: Integrated Composite Stone System (MSAJ)Background: The construction industry has long struggled with the inherent "brittleness" and high mass of natural mineral stones, which leads to structural vulnerabilities and high logistical costs. This invention introduces a novel composite stone system designed to replace traditional brittle materials with an ultra-resistant, steadfast, and lightweight alternative.Methodology: Validated by official laboratory results dated December 27, 2017, this invention utilizes a proprietary fiber-reinforced composite matrix and a capillary stress distribution network. Mechanical testing conducted by the Gamanekav Laboratory confirmed a compressive strength (UCS) of 55.0 MPa and a density of 1.74 $g/cm^3$, which is approximately 34% lighter than natural travertine.Key Features:Structural Integrity: Unlike natural minerals, the system dissipates energy throughout its body, preventing catastrophic failure under impact or structural settling.Operational Efficiency: The "Single Body" stone-block integration allows for simultaneous masonry and facade finishing, increasing execution speed by an estimated factor of 6.Economic Advantage: In the premium countertop market (traditionally priced up to $6,000), this invention provides a luxury aesthetic with zero breakage risk at approximately half the market price for the end consumer.Conclusion: With its capability for "On-Site Mobile Production" and a global licensing model, this invention represents a significant shift toward sustainable, cost-effective, and seismically safe construction materials on a global scale.Keywords & Tags / تگ‌های تخصصیScientific & Technical Tags:#CompositeStone #StructuralRigidity #HighStrengthConcrete #MaterialScienceInvention #FiberReinforcedComposite #CompressiveStrength_55MPa #SeismicResistantMaterialsConstruction & Engineering Tags:#FastTrackConstruction #IntegratedFacade #LightweightBuildingMaterials #SingleBodyMasonry #ModularConstruction #StructuralOptimizationMarket & Business Tags:#PremiumCountertops #GlobalLicensing #OnSiteProduction #ConstructionInnovation #EconomicBuildingSolutions #SustainableArchitecture
