AB  - In India, there is a huge buildup of industrial waste.These waste products, including sugarcane bagasse, marble dust, copper slag, rice husk, and eggshell, are widely used as partial replacements for cement and sand in concrete.Sugarcanebagasse is the name given to the byproduct after sugarcane juice is extracted.The sugarcane bagasse ash is produced when the sugarcane bagasse is carefully burned at a specific temperature.The marble manufacturing industry produces marble dust in abundance.Sand and marble polishing waste both have physical and chemical qualities that are similar to those of marble powder used in construction.This research is based exclusively on experiments focusing on the partial replacement of FA and cement with wastes, BA, and MD in the M25 grade concrete mix.Replacement ratios adapted were 5%, 10%, 15%, and 20%.Curing was done for 7 and 28 days.It was investigated how the partial replacement would affect mechanical qualities i.e. compressive and split-tensile strength.Observations demonstrated that the cement and fine aggregate replacement level of 10% resulted in the best strength gain.The partial replacement of SCBA & MD for cement & fine aggregate improved mechanical strength in concrete.
