AB  - Marble stones are natural rocks that demonstrate special texture, unique patterns and vibrant colour. They are durable and tough, and, hence can be simply formed into several sizes and shape; to be utilized as floor decorative and cladding purpose. An enormous amount of non-biodegradable trash is produced during the mining and processing of dimensional stones like marble. Since it disrupts the ecology in so many ways, this has become a serious issue over time. Finding a method to securely dispose of or reuse marble waste is thus important. There are studies showing that this discarded can be utilized in replacement of conventional building materials. The present review paper investigates the influence of waste marble stone on workability, mechanical and durability characteristics when utilized as partial to full substitution in type of mortar and concrete mixtures. The concluded review of the literature, waste marble stone partial replacement of cement, and partial and full substitution of fine and coarse aggregate has been used to produce mortar and concrete.
