AB  - In this current study investigates the possibility of construction demolish waste (CDW) and waste marble slurry (WMS) as a coarse aggregate (20mm) and cement in the making of concrete. CDW added in (0% to 30% at interval of 10%), and WMS used in (0% to 30% at interval of 10%) to make the concrete blends. Total of four blends was cast including control mixture, and three mixtures for combined use of WMS and CDW. Workability, water absorption, and mechanical strength tests were performed to judge the performance of concrete prepared with WMS and CDW. With WMS and CDW, the workability of concrete was decreased, although within acceptable limits as per the Indian standard code. Concrete blend prepared with combined used of 10% WMS and 10% CDW (i.e. M10C10 blend) displayed maximum compressive and split tensile strength (STS). The results suggested the optimum use of CDW up to 10% and WMS up to 10% as a coarse aggregate and cement replacement in concrete.
