AB  - The concept of a circular economy proposes that industrial waste be used as raw material for making new products to reduce the environmental impact and stimulate economic growth.Thus, many scientific studies and patents have aimed to take advantage of different waste compounds in the development of new composite materials.The goal of this study is to assess the potential for using marble and synthetic fibers for the development of new materials through the analysis of patent documents filed worldwide.We analyzed prospective documents in the Derwent Innovation Index database.A total of 129 documents related to the research area of interest was identified between 1958 and 2019.The construction sector had a higher total number of patents and active patents relative to the industrial sector with a focus on structural, antimicrobial, and covering applications.Japan, the United States, and South Korea were the countries that filed the most patents related to the research topic.
