AB  - Waste management has become one of the most difficult problemto protect the environment for sustainability. Reuse of waste materials saves construction cost and some environmental problems too.In this present research, the waste matter from the iron manufacturing industries, mining industries and demolished building has been used in concrete making. GGBS, Cement is partially replaced with an iron-steel industry waste product in amounts ranging from 0–30% by weight. White marble is a by-product from mines and demolished buildings, where natural granite coarse aggregate is replaced by synthetic material. JSW make slag sand, a by-product from iron and steel manufacturing industries, is used as a 100% replacement of river sand, in M30 grade concrete.Concrete's tensile strength is the topic of this study produced with the incorporation of waste by products for sustainable construction. Compressive, tensile and flexural strengths have been determined and compared with control concrete of M30 Grade. The results are analysed to establish the feasibility of incorporating the industrial wastes in M30 grade concrete.
