AB  - The volcanic rocks are classified as nephelinites, leucitites, basanites and tephrites as well as phonolithes and tuffs. In terms of marketing, the basaltic rocks are, independent of their precise composition, named, for example, Mayener Basaltlava , Mendiger Basaltlava and Plaidter Basaltlava . The lava streams had two central areas: one in the eastern and one in the western part of the Eifel Mountains. Most of the industrial extracted basalt lava is indeed used as aggregates in the asphalt and concrete industry as well as in hydraulic construction. The Rhenish Basalt Lava is very suitable for producing all kinds of ornamental stones and building stones. Microscopically, the basalt lava is characterized by a holocrystalline porphyric structure: inclusions of pyroxene, intensively altered mafic minerals and sporadic olivine are “swimming” in a fine-crystalline homogeneous matrix, a mixture of pyroxene, feldspar, foides and opaque ore minerals. The Rhenish Basalt Lava is resistant to sunburn and during freeze/thaw cycles.
