AU  - Ana Martha Carneiro Pires de Oliveira
AU  - Rodrigo do Val Andrade
PY  - 2020
JO  - Journal of Open Research
UR  - https://stellata.com.br/journals/jor/article/view/24
AB  - The challenge of meeting the requirements for solid waste management generated by many industrial activities finds recycling an economically viable alternative. The ornamental stone industry, among which marble shops produce waste as a result of the process of cutting, polishing, and polishing the pieces. This waste that is difficult to dispose of is a constant concern of marble makers. Ceramic bricks are present in any masonry construction, be it sealing or structural. The research carried on the reuse of ornamental stone residues in the making of ceramic bricks was carried out because this type of material does not have aesthetic restrictions regarding its coloring, as it happens in other segments of the ceramic industry. This study presents the advantages obtained from the addition of ornamental stone residues in the characteristics of water absorption and rupture resistance in bricks. The results indicate that the addition of ornamental stone residues keeps the quality of the bricks. As well, they reduce the bricks production cost by decreasing the demand for raw materials in the execution of the mass that compose them, proving that the use of marble or granite residues is a solution o management of solid waste from the ornamental stone industry.
