TY  - JOUR
TI  - Optimizing the shielding properties of strength-enhanced concrete containing marble
AU  - A. Abdel-Latif M
AU  - M. Kassab
AU  - M.I. Sayyed
AU  - Huseyin Ozan Tekin
PY  - 2020
JO  - Papers in Physics
DO  - 10.4279/pip.120005
UR  - https://doi.org/10.4279/pip.120005
AB  - The purpose of this study is to develop a low cost, locally produced concrete mixture with optimum marble content. The resulting mixture would have enhanced strength properties compared to the non-marble reference concrete, and improved radiation shielding properties. To accomplish these goals five concrete mixtures were prepared, containing 0, 5, 10, 15, and 20% marble waste powder as a cement replacement on the basis of weight.These samples were subjected to a compressive strength test. The shielding parameters such as mass attenuation coefficients μm, mean free path MFP, effective atomic number $Z_{eff}$ and exposure build-up factors EBF were measured, and results were compared with those obtained using the WinXcom program and MCNPX code in the photon energy range of 0.015 - 3 MeV. Moreover, the macroscopic fast neutron removal cross-section (neutron attenuation coefficient) was calculated and the results presented. The results show that the sample which contains 10% marble has the highest compressive strength and potentially good gamma ray and neutron radiation shielding properties.
