AB  - The paper examines methods of assessing the critical fractures and quality of an ornamental stone deposit. Fracture status was evaluated by an in-situ Ground Penetrating Radar (GPR) test. The resulting 3D GPR model allowed exploration of the extension, shape, and orientation of the detected fractures surfaces. It also identified a rock stratum with a noticeably lower load of critical fractures compared to the other strata. Physico-mechanical properties were investigated by laboratory tests allowing classification of the deposit into quality categories, which provided a promising correlation with the GPR survey results.
