TI  - Aproveitamento de resíduos de pedreiras de rochas ornamentais como agregados para base e sub-base de pavimentos
AU  - Hieres Vettorazzi da Silva
AU  - Nuria Fernández Castro
PY  - 2016
UR  - http://mineralis.cetem.gov.br/bitstream/cetem/1956/1/Hieres%20Vettorazzi%20V%20JPCI.pdf
AB  - The materials used for the asphalt pavement base and subbase must have good compressive strength, low deformability and being sufficiently permeable to avoid structural damage to the pavement. Natural stones wastes accumulated in quarries, over decades, are a major environmental liability by both the visual impact as the nappropriate use of natural resources. Generally stored in waste dumps, commonly known in Brazil as bota-fora, their volumes reach thousands of cubic meters. Aiming at sustainable production of ornamental stones, the V Jornada do Programa de Capacitacao Institucional – CETEM 2 main goal of this work is to indicate quarry wastes sites in the State of Espirito Santo that can be utilized in paving the Governor Mario Covas Highway, BR-101, whose duplication is in its initial phase. After an earlier stage of documental selection and GIS mapping, in which 72 potential targets were identified, it was conducted a field work narrowing those to 23 quarries dumps with availability of use, as a function of available volumes and distance to the highway. The second stage, in progress, consisted of sampling of material from the selected quarries and its characterization in the Espirito Santo Regional Unit of the Centre for Mineral Technology - NRES/CETEM/MCTIC. The analysis and relevant tests are still being conducted, but the results so far found, indicate that the use of part of this waste at the BR-101 pavement base is economically and technologically feasible.
