AB  - The aim of this study is the technological characterization of aggregates produced from the crushing and classification of coarse wastes of the natural stones sawing in order to be used in concrete products. Samples of thirteen types of stones’ wastes were selected and collected from an industrial landfill, located in Cachoeiro de Itapemirim-ES. Samples were crushed and the produced aggregates: gravel 0, 1 and crushed stone powder were characterized for particle size, density, water absorption, impact resistance, Los Angeles abrasion resistance, shape index and fineness modulus following Brazilian standards. A commercial Mix produced in the same landfill, was afterwards also collected and characterized. The results obtained with the selected types of rocks indicate that not all materials under study would fit the desirable requirements of NBR 7211. The commercial mix showed good results, but new mixes characterization and testing are still necessary.
