AB  - One of the most important properties for the use of any material as flooring is its slip resistance, since this property is related to safety issues regarding the mobility. In the case of natural stones coverings, the determination of such property is not standardized within the Brazilian Standards scope of testing methods. The objective of this study was to evaluate the reliability of the British pendulum method by estimating the uncertainty of measurement and through the calculation of repeatability and reproducibility. Tests were carried out in laboratory and on the floorings of the Shopping Cachoeiro. The number of samples and measurements necessary for this study was determined through statistical analysis of previous data, considering confidence levels of 95 and 99%. The uncertainties for almost 4,500 measurements were estimated and the repeatability and reproducibility calculated. Initial results of this work showed that this method has good reliability and great potential to be incorporated into the set of Brazilian technical standards.
