AB  - The transformation of the rough stone until the moment it is sold in slabs, tiles and other products, generates large amounts of wastes, fine and coarse. The fine wastes, after being dehydrated are deposited within authorized landfills. These residues have great potential to be utilized in the construction industry, especially in the composition of mortars and concretes. Under this conception, and seeking evidence in laboratory for the positive results already obtained in an actual building site, this work presents the comparative results of three mixtures with different formulations, one with residue of ornamental rocks, in the proportion of 100 kg / cbm. The results, preliminary, are positive for the use of this input, as Ecofiller in pumpable concrete, because of the fluidity of the mixture obtained and its mechanical strengt.
