AB  - With the growth of industries, there is a major concern with the particulate matter suspended in the atmosphere, as metals, soot, dust, among others, and the dimension stone sector has contributed to this growth, even with the use of water in the processes there is still an amount of particles released into the environment. The suspended total particles may contain particles from the process, neighboring localities, road, which may have potential effects on human health and the environment. Thus, this study aimed to characterize the suspended total particles generated in the dimension stones processing by scanning electron microscopy connected to an energy dispersive X-ray spectroscopy system (SEM/EDS) and X-ray diffraction (XRD). Particulate samples were collected in a company using large-volume sampler (Hivol). Measurements were realized near the multiblade gang saws, multiwire gang saws and polishing, in order to obtain results of particulates that are emitted in the processes to be inserted in the life-cycle inventory of dimension stones.
