AB  - The aim of this study was to investigate the effects of waste generated in the marble industry on acidic soil neutralization by column tests in a laboratory. Furthermore, field trials were conducted to determine the effects of marble wastes on hazelnut yield. As marble wastes, both marble quarry wastes and marble cutting wastes, are rich in CaCO3, they were used as a pH regulator for acidic soil. In this way, not only the wastes were utilized as a useful raw material for the agriculture but also the burden of marble wastes on the environment was reduced. The results showed that soil pH increased from 4.71 to 6.84 in column tests and hazelnut yield increased 43% in the field trials upon marble waste application
