AB  - The essay studies the marble building materials found in the archeological digs of Asturica Augusta between 1971 and 1994. The combination of petrography and cathodoluminescence have identified the major use of different ornamental stones from Leon (pink and cream limestone griottes from Lancara Formation, white limestones from Vegadeo, white and grey marbles from Cuevas del Sil and San Fiz and maroon limestone from Cantabrian mountains), also white and grey portuguese marbles from Estremoz Anticline, Viana do Alentejo and Trigaches. Its use, since Augustian period, became widespread between Claude and the Flavians. Also, it discusses the possible approaches, according to the different hypotheses made by some authors.
