TI  - Epidemiological Survey of Silicosis in Granite Stone Material Processing Industry
AU  - Feng Zhou
PY  - 2011
JO  - Zhiye yu jiankang
UR  - https://en.cnki.com.cn/Article_en/CJFDTOTAL-ZYJK201124001.htm
AB  - [Objective]To investigate the incidence and pathogenesis regularity of silicosis in granite stone material processing industry,to predict the epidemic trend,and provide scientific evidence for developing control measures. [Methods]The retrospective survey was adopted to collect the silicosis case data from this industry during January 1963-December 2010 with survey plan.The data were used to form a database and analyzed with SPSS 17.0. [Results]During 47 years,the number of accumulative reported cases in the industry was 118,Among them,78(66.10%) were pneumoconiosis stage I,35(29.66%) of stage II,and 5(4.24%) of stage III.The types of work with risk of silicosis were stonecutter(81.51%),drillman(9.24%),haulageman(1.68%) and other works(7.56%).The average service length of onset was about 34 years,and the average onset age was about 55 years. [Conclusion]The number of sillicosis cases increased during 1960-1980,and significantly decreased from 1990,and no new cases appeared after 2000.It suggests that the monitoring and risk control of dust hazard must be enhanced,and health surveillance system should be established for dust exposure population.
