AB  - The classification of Chinese ornamental stones is based on their ornamental features, and there are four major categories according to the natural shapes, sizes, ornamental characteristics and appreciation ways, namely natural scenic stones, garden stones, supply stones, and other stones. And each major category is further divided into a number of species and types. As if the ornamental stone culture is a giant tree, then the four major categories is like the main trunks propping up the tremendous crown, while the colorful, ever-changing stones are the lush foliage and fruits. Eight key elements are essential for stone appreciation: image, quality, color, texture, rhythm, conception, naming, and pedestal. The integration of these eight aspects is the standard.
