AB  - Exceed 152 various active Dimension Stone (DS) quarries extracting by means of diamond wire are scattered throughout West Azerbaijan province in Iran. In this manner, incomes due to DS quarrying will affectively increase providing that costs of the diamond wire consumption and consequently specific cut (cutting planes per the unit of DS volume or weight) decrease. Therefore, in this study attempts have been made to minimize specific cut so that a computerized procedure is pursued. The assembled data from the 110 working faces were employed during the computerized procedure design. Consequently, for the purpose that the specific cuts might be impressively reduced, an optimal shape and size of minableblocks were attained.
