TY  - JOUR
TI  - Ceramic Glaze Preparation with K-Feldspar Granite Waste
AU  - WU Hai-lin
PY  - 2009
JO  - Journal of Guilin University of Technology
UR  - https://en.cnki.com.cn/Article_en/CJFDTotal-GLGX200904018.htm
AB  - The possibility of K-feldspar granite waste as raw materials for ceramic glaze is studied.The glazes are made by intergrinding 80% K-feldspar granite,20% wollastonite and 0.2% sodium carboxymethyl cellulose.The K-feldspar granite waste is characterized by differential thermal analysis(DTA) and X-ray diffraction(XRD),and the fineness of glazes by granulometer.Scanning electron microscope(SEM) is employed to examine the microstructure of the glazes surface.Glossiness and microhardness of the glazes are tested.The experiment indicates that the ceramic glazes are strong body-glaze fit with good property when D97 is 34.86 μm and firing temperature is between 1 200 ℃ and 1 300 ℃.The surface of glaze is smooth and the glossiness is 82% to 93%.The range of microhardness is from 590.1 to 604.5 MPa.
