AB  - Marble waste, in the form of sludge obtained from the marble cutting industry, was incorporated in the mixture formulations of concrete block.The possibility of using marble sludge powders (MSPs) as a substitute for limestone was investigated over a three year period.The production of cement block from sludge was standardised in terms of process and content.Interpretation of the results have shown that appropriate incorporation of MSP can result in favourable characteristics in terms of compression strength 9 N/nm 2 at 28 days, and water absorption (7%), anticipating a complimentary usage of sludge as a by-product instead of being waste.
