AB  - Economic and environmental obstacles and regulations constraints to assure cultural sustainability of ornamental stones. “Cultural sustainability of stones” has to be intended as the capability of stones, of which monuments and art masterpieces are made , to preserve, maintain and transmit to future generations the cultural message they contain. To achieve this objective, the priorities should be to protect and preserve the world’s artistic and architectural historical heritage, through the study and availability of historical ornamental stones, of which it is essential to discover the location of the original quarry sites: only there, in fact, it will be possible to extract the even small quantities of stones that are needed for restoration works. In the last years the general perception about this subject, in which the extractive industry is going to play an important role, has dramatically improved. In parallel, land planning and environmental management instruments, like ISO 14001 Environmental Management Systems, have been developed, that should support the task of mining activity. Substantial problems, however, exist when historical stones have in practice to be supplied. These problems consist of economic and environmental obstacles, to which regulation constraints have to be added, due to the fact that, in general, the minimum conditions requested to start and manage a normal industrial activity do not exist. In the paper, the situation of historical marble is considered with reference to the case of an historical marble district in southern Piedmont, and a possible solution is proposed.
