AB  - Some building ornamental materials with yellow black veins and based on the spodumene and the residual slag of Pb Zn mineral have been prepared by conventional melt quenching technology. The physicochemical property and the structure of these materials are investigated by using X ray diffraction and SEM methods and the differences of the properties between the building materials and the natural stone materials are studied. The results show that the materials are non crystal and contain a large number of partial melts SiO 2 or Al 2O 3 particles with 0.2 μm. The properties and the esthetic effects are similar to those of the natural stone materials.
