TY  - JOUR
TI  - The transformation of ornamental stones in Portugal
AU  - António Travassos
PY  - 2000
UR  - https://www.voced.edu.au/content/ngv%3A5581
AB  - This provisional study of the ornamental stone transformation sector in Portugal is part of a series of sectorial studies within the framework of the ‘Evolution in Qualifications and Diagnostic of Training Needs’ project. It constitutes a reference in terms of strategic information and aims to provide a socio-economic and technical-organisational characterisation that allows the analysis of qualifications and sustains the diagnostic of training needs. The study results indicate: (1) the diagnostic of the sector relating to employment, the options it has in terms of markets and product strategies, the technological configuration and human resource management, and their effects on qualifications and skills; (2) the scenarios for the evolution of these factors and their effect on employment, qualifications and skills; (3) the construction of professional profiles based on both the present jobs as well as target jobs; (4) the survey and a brief analysis of the training network; (5) the identification of training needs; and (6) the identification of other interventions necessary to compensate possible lack of skills and increase the competitiveness of the sector. The chapters are: Delimitation of the sector of transformation of ornamental stone; Diagnostic of the sector of transformation of ornamental stone; Evolution of jobs, qualifications and professional skills; Diagnostic of training needs and pointers for the reorientation of professional training; Conclusions and other strategies to respond to skill needs. This study also includes a supplement containing professional profiles, scenarios and specification of the levels of knowledge.
