TY  - JOUR
TI  - ENVIRONMENTALLY FRIENDLY TECHNOLOGIES FOR DIMENSION STONE DEPOSIT DEVELOPMENT
AU  - V. KALIUZHNA
PY  - 1998
JO  - Матеріали міжнародної науково-практиченої конференції Екологія Людина Суспільство
DO  - 10.20535/ehs2710-3315.1998.371653
UR  - https://doi.org/10.20535/ehs2710-3315.1998.371653
AB  - Environmentally oriented technologies for developing dimension-stone deposits were considered with regard to natural properties of the rock mass and controllable mining parameters. Productivity and waste generation were shown to depend on deposit geometry, natural jointing, rock structure and texture, mineralogical composition, and physical-mechanical properties of the stone. For each rock mass, the orientation of joint systems should be determined and the direction of the working front coordinated with them, as this affects the size and quality of extracted blocks. The choice of monolith separation method was related to rock type: wedge-and-drill methods may be suitable for some rocks, while continuous drilling is preferable for others. Accounting for natural blockiness and grain size can reduce breakage of marketable stone and the volume of off-grade waste. Quarry productivity was proposed to be treated as a function of uncontrollable natural and controllable technological factors. Optimizing their combination should increase marketable yield while reducing environmental disturbance.
