AB  - Blue pectolite from the Dominican Republic, also known by the trade name Larimar, has recently entered the U.S. market.Large quantities of this attractive ornamental stone have been found i n cavities and veins of altered basalt.Most of the gemologiccil properties are consistent with those previously reported for pectolite; the cause of color in this material is believed to be related to the presence of small amounts of Cu2+.The color appears to be stable to light, but does react to irradiation and to the heat of a jeweler's torch.It is easily separated from similar-appearing materials.
