TY  - JOUR
TI  - DEVELOPMENT OF REALISTIC TEST PROCEDURES
AU  - Harald Haas
PY  - 1977
UR  - https://trid.trb.org/view/1064838
AB  - THE AUTHOR DESCRIBES THE SPECIFIC FIELD OF ACTIVITY OF TEST LABORATORIES IN THE BUILDING CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY, WHICH PARTICULARLY NEED TO REPRODUCE THE REQUIREMENTS OF CONSTRUCTION PRACTICE. FOR THIS PURPOSE IT IS NECESSARY TO UTILIZE TEST PROCEDURES AND EQUIPMENT WHICH QUICKLY, SAFELY AND WITHOUT GREAT EXPENDITURE PRODUCE THE APPROPRIATE TEST RESULTS. THE AUTHOR DESCRIBES FOUR METHODS WITH WHICH HE HAS BEEN ASSOCIATED DURING THEIR DEVELOPMENT IN THE CENTRAL LABORATORIES OF STRABAG BAU-AG AND WHICH HAVE SINCE BECOME WIDELY KNOWN AMONGST SPECIALISTS: (1) PROCEDURE AND APPARATUS FOR THE DETERMINATION OF THE FINE AGGREGATE CONSTITUENT OF COARSE GRAINED SOILS AND BUILDING MATERIALS, WHICH HAS BEEN INCLUDED IN THE PUBLICATION NOTES ON SOIL TEST PROCEDURES IN HIGHWAY CONSTRUCTION. IT POSSESSES ADVANTAGES OVER THE SIEVE AND WASHING ANALYSES SO THAT ITS HIGHER DEGREE OF ACCURACY FULFILS PRACTICAL REQUIREMENTS. (2) THE DENSITOMETER (WATER REPLACEMENT METHOD) FOR THE DETERMINATION OF DENSITY OF SOILS AND BULK MATERIALS REPLACES THE SAND REPLACEMENT METHOD WHICH HAD PREVIOUSLY BEEN EXCLUSIVELY USED AND POSSESSES A NUMBER OF ADVANTAGES WHICH ITS USE REINFORCES AND REMOVES THE UNCERTAINTIES ASSOCIATED WITH THE USE OF ISOTOPE MEASURING EQUIPMENT. IT HAS BEEN STANDARDIZED IN DIN 18125, PAGE 2. (3) AN IMPACT TESTING MACHINE FOR NATURAL STONE AGGREGATE DESIGNED FOR USE ON CONSTRUCTION SITES. THE GENERALLY USED IMPACT TESTING OF AGGREGATE 8/12 FOLLOWING THE APPROPRIATE CODE HAS KNOWN DISADVANTAGES. IT IS REFERRED TO IN THE CONFIRMATION OF THE SINGLE SIZE IMPACT TEST AS AN EMPIRICALLY DEVELOPED APTITUDE AND CONTROL TEST PROCEDURE WITH GOOD REPRODUCTIVE QUALITIES AND IS MENTIONED IN THE RECENTLY OPERATED RING INVESTIGATIONS, THE RESULTS OF WHICH ARE STILL AWAITED. (4) THE HYDROMETER CONTAINER FOR THE MEASUREMENT OF CRUDE DENSITY OF COARSE GRAINED SOILS AND BUILDING MATERIALS. THE AIR PICNOMETER IS UNABLE TO PROVIDE SUFFICIENTLY ACCURATE RESULTS OF THE PORE VOLUME AS REQUIRED BY STANDARD ZTVE-STB 65. THE NEW, ALREADY ESTABLISHED, APPARATUS IS INCLUDED IN THE REVISED EDITION OF NOTES ON SOIL TEST PROCEDURES.
