AB  - LOWER SILESIAN SERPENTINITES AND POSSIBILITIES OF THEIR USE AS ORNAMENTAL STONES

Summary
The paper presents geological-mineralogical characteristics of the Lower Silesian serpentinites with regard to the Possibility of their use as ornamental stones. Serpentinites from the deposits occurring in the vicinities of Jordanow Śląski, Naslawice, Radunia hills (Tąpadla area) and Zloty Stok area have been found the most suitable for ornamentation purposes. They may be used in the production of artistic-ornamentational objects for both – home market and export.
