AB  - Study of thirteen cores and a hand specimen taken from the dimension stone of the Salt Lake City and County Building indicates that the weathering results mainly from mechanical rather than chemical processes. Penetration of water into the stone with alternate freezing and thawing is considered to be the most important process at work.
